      "post_subject": "High resolution PVA polymer",
      "content_md": "I have found an article that shows a recipe for a PVA+Acrylamide+MethBisAcrylamide+Acrylic Acid+TEA+MB solution that has a sensitivity of 50mJ/cm and a resolution of more than 3000 lines per mm.\n\nThe article calls for a PVA with a very low molecular weight of 9000 and states that PVA with higher molecular weights don't work with resolutions higher than 2000 lines per mm.\n\nThe PVA with the lowest Molecular Weight I have found thus far is 3-98. That has a MW of 16000 and is still much too high.\n\nDoes anyone know where I cound find PVA with MW 9000?\n\n(p.s. The article claims a real-time diffraction efficiency of 85% in a 20um film, exposed in red HeNe light!!!)",
      "signature": "",
      "attachments": [],
      "quotes": [],
      "is_first_post": true,
